<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A slur over three noteheads: the notation for a melisma — one syllable sung across several
  notes — which is the app's name and the thing its renderer draws letter by letter. The three
  dots are the interlude marker the renderer already shows between vocal lines.

  Drawn inside the central 66dp a launcher mask is guaranteed to keep, and sat 4dp above the
  geometric centre: the dots are compact and the slur is thin, so a mark centred by its bounding
  box reads as sitting too low.
-->
